## The user
Product-side, not an engineer. Native Armenian speaker. Hands-off — keep going
autonomously, don't ask "what's next".

## Non-negotiable rules
1. **ARMENIAN-FIRST.** All chat/explanations to the user in Armenian. English only
   for code, paths, URLs, proper names. Explain every technical term in plain Armenian.
2. **DEPLOY FLOW.** Edit locally → `git commit` → `git push origin main`. Pushing
   auto-deploys: backend→Hetzner (GitHub Actions ~12s), admin+frontend→Vercel (~5min).
   Never deploy to Hetzner/Vercel directly — only push to GitHub.
3. **ADMIN PUSH GATE.** Before pushing `zulu-admin-next`, run `npm run lint` AND
   `npx tsc --noEmit` (no `--skipLibCheck`) and confirm both pass clean. ONE ESLint error
   silently blocks the whole Vercel deploy (old bundle keeps serving, curl still 200).
   Verify the real change with a login + screenshot, never trust a curl 200.
4. **ONE REPO PER COMMIT.** Never mix files from different sub-repos in one commit.
   Root `D:/zulu-platform` and `docs/` are NOT git repos.
5. **FIGMA = ASK FIRST.** Before editing any UI/design, ask the user for the Figma
   frame URL. Verify pixel-by-pixel (text, brands, counts).
6. **FIX IN PLACE, NEVER DELETE** UI/content unprompted. "X is messed up" = fix.
7. **HETZNER ARTISAN as www-data:** `sudo -u www-data php artisan ...`, never root.
8. **git in sub-repos:** `git -C <path> ...`, never `cd <path> && git ...`.
9. After raw SQL inserts to `ui_translations`, run `cache:forget ui_translations_<lang>`.
10. **SELF-VERIFY UI** with Playwright (screenshot + console). Save shots to
    `docs/scrinshots/`. Super-admin test login: `claude.admin@zulu.am`.
11. **CYCLE MODE.** Work continuously; make engineering decisions yourself. Escalate
    only business/scope/Figma decisions, destructive prod ops, or deploy.yml changes.

